://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3461#issue-5897047662)\n\nIssue body actions\n\n## Task\n\nPlease implement a \"Hello World\" program in Scala.\n\n## Requirements\n\n1.  Create a file with the appropriate extension for Scala\n2.  The program should print exactly: `Hello, World!`\n3.  Add clear comments explaining the code\n4.  Ensure the code follows Scala best practices and idioms\n5.  If applicable, include build/run instructions in a comment at the top of the file\n6.  **Create a GitHub Actions workflow that automatically runs and tests the program on every push and pull request**\n\n## Expected Output\n\nWhen the program runs, it should output:\n\n```\nHello, World!\n```\n\n## GitHub Actions Requirements\n\nThe CI/CD workflow should:\n\n-   Trigger on push to main branch and on pull requests\n-   Set up the appropriate Scala runtime/compiler\n-   Run the Hello World program\n-   Verify the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n-   Show a green check mark when tests pass\n\nExample workflow structure:\n\n-   Checkout code\n-   Setup Scala environment\n-   Run the program\n-   Assert output matches expected string\n\n## Additional Notes\n\n-   The implementation should be simple and straightforward\n-   Focus on clarity and correctness\n-   Use the standard library only (no external dependencies unless absolutely necessary for Scala)\n-   The GitHub Actions workflow should be in `ci/` directory\n-   The workflow should have a meaningful name like `test-hello-world.yml`\n-   Save the workflow as `ci/test-hello-world.yml`, not under `.github/workflows/`: this repository's token cannot push workflow files, so the test harness copies it there and runs it\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n-    Program file created with correct extension\n-    Code prints \"Hello, World!\" exactly\n-    Code is properly commented\n-    Code follows Scala conventions\n-    Instructions for running the program are included (if needed)\n-    GitHub Actions workflow created and passing\n-    CI badge showing build status (optional but recommended)\n\nReactions are currently unavailable\n\n## Activity\n\n1.  [![](https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?s=64&v=4)github-actions](/apps/github-actions)\n    \n    added\n    \n    [e2e-taskIsolated automation fixture](/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22e2e-task%22)Isolated automation fixture\n    \n    [no-formal-ai-draftIsolated automation fixture](/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22no-formal-ai-draft%22)Isolated automation fixture\n    \n    [on Oct 17, 2026](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3461#event-33513512569)\n    \n\n[Sign up for free](/signup?return_to=https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3461) **to join this conversation on GitHub.** Already have an account? [Sign in to comment](/login?return_to=https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues/3461)\n\n## Metadata\n\n## Metadata\n\n### Assignees\n\nNo one assigned\n\n### Labels\n\n[e2e-taskIsolated automation fixture](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22e2e-task%22)Isolated automation fixture[no-formal-ai-draftIsolated automation fixture](https://github.com/link-assistant/hive-mind/issues?q=state%3Aopen%20label%3A%22no-formal-ai-draft%22)Isolated automation fixture\n\n### Type\n\nNo type\n\n### Projects\n\nNo projects\n\n### Milestone\n\nNo milestone\n\n### Relationships\n\nNone yet\n\n### Development\n\nNo branches or pull requests\n\n## Issue actions\n\n-   ![](https://github.githubassets.com/assets/github-copilot-app-light-15ad5534265eeacd.svg)Open in GitHub Copilot app\n\n## Footer\n\n[](https://github.com)© 2026 GitHub, Inc.\n\n### Footer navigation\n\n-   [Terms](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/github-terms/github-terms-of-service)\n-   [Privacy](https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement)\n-   [Security](https://github.com/security)\n-   [Status](https://www.gi