request, set up Scala, run the program, and verify output.\\n\\nLet's first check if there's any existing Scala structure. We'll create the file in the root or maybe in a src directory? The issue doesn't specify a directory structure, so we can put it in the root.\\n\\nWe'll create:\\n- HelloWorld.scala\\n- ci/test-hello-world.yml\\n\\nLet's start by creating the Scala file.\",\"format\":\"unknown\",\"index\":0}]},{\"role\":\"tool\",\"tool_call_id\":\"call-55e2b535-9776-4a29-8474-d31900ef5133\",\"content\":\"[\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Create HelloWorld.scala file that prints 'Hello, World!'\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"in_progress\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"1\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add comments and follow Scala best practices\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"2\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Create GitHub Actions workflow in ci/test-hello-world.yml\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"3\\\"\\n  },\\n  {\\n    \\\"content\\\": \\\"Verify the workflow runs and passes\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"pending\\\",\\n    \\\"priority\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n    \\\"id\\\": \\\"4\\\"\\n  }\\n]\",\"name\":\"todowrite\"},{\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":null,\"tool_calls\":[{\"id\":\"call-f8cf817a-4465-4813-8047-17953ccdb941\",\"type\":\"function\",\"function\":{\"name\":\"write\",\"arguments\":\"{\\\"content\\\":\\\"/**\\\\n * HelloWorld.scala\\\\n * \\\\n * A simple Scala program that prints \\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\" to the console.\\\\n * \\\\n * To run this program:\\\\n *   scala HelloWorld.scala\\\\n * \\\\n * Or compile and run:\\\\n *   scalac HelloWorld.scala\\\\n *   scala HelloWorld\\\\n */\\\\n\\\\nobject HelloWorld {\\\\n  def main(args: Array[String]): Unit = {\\\\n    println(\\\\\\\"Hello, World!\\\\\\\")\\\\n  }\\\\n}\\\",\\\"filePath\\