[2026-10-17T09:43:34.391Z] [INFO]     "text": "I have successfully implemented the Hello World program in Scala and created the required GitHub Actions workflow. Here's a summary of what was accomplished:\n\n## Changes Made\n\n1. **Created `HelloWorld.scala`**:\n   - A simple Scala object with a `main` method that prints \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Includes clear comments explaining the code and how to run it\n   - Follows Scala best practices and idioms\n\n2. **Created `ci/test-hello-world.yml`**:\n   - GitHub Actions workflow that triggers on push and pull requests to the main branch\n   - Sets up Scala (version 3.3.0) using the official `scala-lang/setup-scala` action\n   - Runs the Scala program and verifies the output is exactly \"Hello, World!\"\n   - Saved in the `ci/` directory as requested\n\n## Pull Request Status\n- Updated PR #3462 with the implementation\n- Changed title from \"[WIP] Implement Hello World in Scala\" to \"Implement Hello World in Scala\"\n- Updated description with detailed summary of changes and verification steps\n- Marked PR as ready for review\n- Confirmed base branch is correctly set to `e2e/hello-world/39021281642/agent-nemotron-3-super-free`\n\n## Verification\nThe workflow will automatically:\n- Checkout the code\n- Set up the Scala environment\n- Run `HelloWorld.scala`\n- Verify the output matches \"Hello, World!\" exactly\n\nAll requirements from issue #3461 have been fulfilled. The CI will run automatically on every push and pull request to ensure the program works correctly.",
